# The campaign's raw output is ~21 MB per run and is REGENERATED by run.sh --
# committing it would put three copies of a machine-readable blob into a
# library's history forever to preserve something a script reproduces.
campaign.raw
results/campaign.json
results/campaign-tce-on.json

# Intermediates derived from the above by disposition.py / the re-grade driver.
# Re-grade inputs: slices of campaign.json, regenerated in seconds by
# disposition.py --emit-input / sample-kills.py. authoritative-input.json
# alone is 6.1 MB.
results/*-input.json
results/survivors.json
results/unreviewed.txt
results/unreviewed/
results/*.log
results/*.err

# Kept in git deliberately, because they are the EVIDENCE the ledger cites and
# nothing regenerates them without re-running the whole campaign:
#   results/verified-authoritative.json -- the serial full-suite re-grade the
#     dispositions rest on, and the only one disposition.py reads
#   results/verified-unrev.json -- the repeat-run evidence that the current
#     re-grade harness is deterministic
#   results/equivalent.json  -- the bytecode-equivalence proofs
#   results/dispositions.md  -- the per-mutant disposition table (criterion 4)
#   results/spans.json       -- the doc/api/raise line spans triage rests on

# Output of the two DEFECTIVE re-grade harnesses (STATUS.md has the table): v1
# manufactured kills, v2 manufactured survivals. The findings are written up in
# prose with their named reproductions -- `type_decoder.ex:349` and
# `abi.ex:674` -- and these blobs add nothing a reader would open. Kept on disk,
# out of a published library's history.
results/verified.json
results/verified-pass*.json
results/verified-v2-DISCARDED.json
